  "about": "An office floor: what it is for, the part every kind of office shares. Its uses in groups by what people do there (arrival, individual work, working together, social and care, support, technical, wet, core, site), each with the firm's smallest sizes and what it holds. Planned from people: desks are shared by 1.2 people (CBRE 2025: most organisations aim at 1.01 to 1.49) at about 10 m² a person (BCO 2023). Working together about 0.4 seats a desk (CBRE's average 0.39), focus 0.1. The codes the firm works to (toilets, crèche, accessibility) come with its standards, not here. A variant (Workplace: tech and the rest) extends it.",
